.SS "int p4est_bsearch_partition (\fBp4est_gloidx_t\fP target, const \fBp4est_gloidx_t\fP * gfq, int nmemb)"

.PP
Given target, find index p such that \fCgfq[p] <= target < gfq[p + 1]\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The value that is searched in \fIgfq\fP\&. \fItarget\fP has to satisfy \fCgfq[0] <= target < gfq[nmemb]\fP\&. 
.br
\fIgfq\fP The sorted array (ascending) in that the function will search\&. 
.br
\fInmemb\fP Number of entries in array MINUS ONE\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Index p such that \fCgfq[p] <= target < gfq[p + 1]\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
This function differs from \fBp4est_find_partition\fP since \fBp4est_find_partition\fP searches for two targets using binary search in an optimized way but \fBp4est_bsearch_partition\fP only performs a single binary search\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "unsigned p4est_comm_checksum (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, unsigned local_crc, size_t local_bytes)"

.PP
Compute a parallel partition-independent checksum out of local checksums\&. This checksum depends on the global refinement topology\&. It does not depend on how the mesh is partitioned\&. The result is available on all processors\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The MPI information of this \fBp4est\fP will be used\&. 
.br
\fIlocal_crc\fP Locally computed adler32 checksum\&. 
.br
\fIlocal_bytes\fP Number of bytes used for local checksum\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Parallel checksum on all processors\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p4est_comm_count_pertree (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_gloidx_t\fP * pertree)"

.PP
Compute and distribute the cumulative number of quadrants per tree\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP This \fBp4est\fP needs to have correct values for global_first_quadrant and global_first_position\&. 
.br
\fIpertree\fP On input, memory for num_trees + 1 numbers\&. On output, the cumulative quadrant counts\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBExamples\fP
.in +1c
\fBparticles/particles2\&.c\fP\&.
